# CI on every push (W1-40, CAP-39.a; DEC-075, DEC-087, DEC-489): the deterministic checks, and the evidence
# record of the commit that is built.
#
# The job runs every check `gov check` runs but the declared checks of a tier above G2 (`gov ci job`), gitleaks
# and the project's tests. The checks of `gov check` that carry no tier (openspec, skill version, readiness, the
# policy keys) run at neither hook: the job is the one place for them, and it takes each status as `gov check`
# gives it. It never runs a G3 check: G3 runs in the pre-push hook on the developer's machine (lefthook.yml),
# which leaves the evidence record.
#
# The evidence record is a git note on the head commit, under a ref of its own: refs/notes/gov-evidence.
# The pre-push hook writes and pushes it. A fresh checkout brings no notes, so the job fetches that ref itself
# and `gov ci record` reads the note of the commit it builds. The job fails when the ref cannot be fetched, when
# the commit has no note, when the note cannot be read or names another commit, and when it says failed.
# For a note that says "no G3 check declared" the job prints those words and fails too, until package P-6 is
# decided: the one line that decides it is ACCEPTED in src/gov/ci/command.py.
#
# A result is measured or it is refused (DEC-449, DEC-454): a tool that is not on the runner fails its step.

name: ci

on: push

permissions:
  contents: read

jobs:
  deterministic:
    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
    steps:
      - name: Checkout
        uses: actions/checkout@11bd71901bbe5b1630ceea73d27597364c9af683  # v4.2.2

      # PLACE: TOOLS ON THE RUNNER (package P-4, the owner's; not decided).
      # The steps that put `gov` (this package), gitleaks and pytest on the runner go here, each registered
      # tool at the version and checksum governance/project/tool-registry.yaml records (DEC-083, DEC-287).
      # Until they are here the steps below fail on the hosted runner: the tools are absent.

      - name: Checks of gov check, but the declared ones of a tier above G2
        run: gov ci job

      - name: gitleaks over the commits of the checkout
        run: gitleaks git --config .gitleaks.toml --no-banner --redact --verbose --log-level error

      - name: Tests of the project
        run: python3 -m pytest tests

      # PLACE: ADAPTER COMPARISON (W1-38, rulesync drift; not merged).
      # The step that compares the generated adapters with their sources goes here.

      - name: Fetch the ref of the evidence record
        run: git fetch origin +refs/notes/gov-evidence:refs/notes/gov-evidence

      - name: Evidence record of the commit that is built
        run: gov ci record
